  <prompt>
    BLOCKED ON CORE R2 PHASE A0. Assistant-drafted content must land in the Compose editor as a transient
    working draft, materialized ledger-first (ADR-040): the structured `compose`-disposition SessionOutput
    is written to the session ledger BEFORE any render, and the client materializes the editor content from
    the stored ledger entry (never from a client-only payload). This consumes the core's `ComposeDisposition
    v1` (+ SSE frame) exactly as specified in the handoff doc §1 — it does NOT invent a local disposition or
    payload path. Because the contract is unpublished, this task is authored against the handoff §1 shapes
    and MUST NOT be executed against a guessed shape.
  </prompt>

  <role>
    Full-stack developer fluent in the Spaarke session ledger (ADR-040), the `compose`-disposition SSE side
    channel (ADR-033 `DocumentStreamWriter`), and the Compose editor materialization seam. You consume a
    published core contract; you never fork it.
  </role>

  <goal>
    "Draft an engagement letter into Compose" writes a `compose`-disposition SessionOutput to the ledger,
    emits the core SSE frame (ledger_ref + disposition, not the payload as source of truth), and the client
    materializes the drafted content into the editor from the stored ledger entry — refresh-durable, carrying
    `{bindingId}@t{n}` provenance.
  </goal>

  <context>
    <background>
      Handoff §1 (`ComposeDisposition v1`): (1) `compose` disposition enum member; (2) payload shape
